new file mode 100644
index 0000000..756f1d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/CANVAS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,162 @@
+# Felucca Canvas: a granular canvas engine for the M-VAVE FM-1
+
+This fork of [Felucca](https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca) adds **CANVAS**, a granular engine laid out like a
+touch-grid granular instrument: eight sample columns, each split into eight cells from top (the sample's start) to
+bottom (its end). You place cells on the canvas, and held notes emit grains from the placed cells.
+
+Everything else in Felucca is unchanged: the other 13 engines, the four tracks, the sequencer, FX, projects, the web
+installer and editor. CANVAS appears in the engine list right after GRAIN.
+
+> Unofficial firmware. Not affiliated with M-VAVE, Hügelton Instruments or any granular-synth maker. You install it
+> at your own risk; back up your projects and presets first (the web editor's backup).
+
+## Playing it
+
+1. Pick a track, hold **EDIT** and press the white key for **CNVS** (the tenth engine key, A4), or turn the PRESETS knob
+   to a CANVAS sound (DIAGONAL, CLOUDS, STRIKES, CHECKER, DRONE, RETRO).
+2. Play notes. **C4 plays each sample at its own speed**; other notes transpose it, as on a sampler.
+3. Each grain comes from one placed cell, picked at random. An empty canvas is silent.
+
+## The CANVAS page (EDIT, tap again after EDIT 2)
+
+```
+ COL 3/8   ROW 4/8   CELL ON   SCAN ALL        <- the four knobs
+ ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
+ │ ▢ ▢ ■ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢                      │   ■ placed cell   ▣ emitting right now (accent colour)
+ │ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢   8 columns          │   ◻ the cursor (ringed)
+ │ ...               = 8 samples        │
+ │ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ▢ ■   8 rows = position  │
+ │ CELLS 8                         MIX  │   placed count, SRC
+ └──────────────────────────────────────┘
+ COLUMN 3                      [KEYS] CELLS
+```
+
+| Control | Does |
+| --- | --- |
+| KNOB 1 COL | The cursor's column (1..8) |
+| KNOB 2 ROW | The cursor's row (1..8; 1 is the sample's start) |
+| KNOB 3 CELL | Turn right to place a cell at the cursor, left to clear it |
+| KNOB 4 SCAN | Moves every placed cell one row down (right) or up (left) per detent, wrapping. The canvas slides through the samples |
+| White keys F3..F4 | The cursor column's rows 1..8. A press toggles that cell; the key's light shows that the cell is placed. These eight keys are silent on this page |
+| The other keys | Play as usual, so you can edit cells while a chord rings |
+| PRESETS knob | Does nothing on this page (a sound load would replace your canvas) |
+
+Off the CANVAS page, all keys play normally.
+
+## Parameters
+
+**EDIT 1**
+
+| | | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| SRC | MIX, PIANO, FLUTE, SAX, USR1..3 | What the eight columns play. MIX: eight different built-in zones. A set: its zones in turn. USR1..3: the zones you uploaded with the web editor (zones 1..8; a slot with fewer repeats them). An empty slot is silent |
+| SIZE | 10 ms .. ~0.66 s | Grain length |
+| DENS | 1 .. ~98 grains/s per voice | Grain rate |
+| SPRY | 0..127 | Random spread from the cell's start. 0: exactly the cell's start. ~32: anywhere in the cell. 127: about four cells down. Also jitters the timing |
+
+**EDIT 2**
+
+| | | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| PTCH | ±24 semitones | Transpose |
+| RAND | 0..127 | Random detune per grain (up to ±1 octave at 127) |
+| TONE | 0..127 | Low-pass (127 open) |
+| SKIP | 0..127 | Chance a grain is left out (127: almost all) |
+
+HOME's knobs are SIZE, DENS, SPRY and SRC.
+
+**Modulation.** LFO or ENV → **SHP** (LFO DEST, ENV DEST or the MOD matrix) scans every grain's position through
+the whole sample, wrapping. Slow LFO → SHP is the classic moving-playhead texture. FLT modulation moves TONE.
+
+The ADSR (ENV page), FX sends, INSERT, voice modes, ARP and the sequencer all work as with any engine. Up to
+4 voices; up to 16 grains per track.
+
+## What is saved
+
+The canvas belongs to the sound:
+
+- **Projects and the autosave.** A CANVAS track stores its 64 cells in the project's per-track FM6-patch area (a
+  CANVAS track has no FM6 patch). When such a project loads, that track's FM6 patch resets to the init voice, which
+  only matters if you later switch that track to FM6.
+- **User presets** (SAVE > USER). Stored beside the record, as FM6 patches are.
+- **Undo.** SAVE held after a sound load brings the cells back.
+- **Factory presets.** Each has its own canvas.
+
+**Favourites.** FAV doesn't stick on CANVAS's factory presets: Felucca's favourites table has no free byte left for
+a sixteenth engine. Save the sound as a user preset and star that instead.
+
+Live parameter editing from the web editor sees CANVAS's eight parameters but not the cells. Full backups made with
+the web editor include them (they live in the project and user-preset objects).
+
+## Installing from a browser (no build on your computer)
+
+The repository carries a GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/pages.yml`) that builds the firmware in the cloud
+and publishes Felucca's web installer with it on GitHub Pages:
+
+1. Create a GitHub repository and upload this source to its `main` branch.
+2. In the repository: **Settings > Pages > Build and deployment > Source: GitHub Actions**.
+3. **Actions > Build and publish installer > Run workflow** (it also runs on every push). It takes a few minutes.
+4. Open `https://<your-user>.github.io/<repo>/webapp/installer/` in **Chrome or Edge** (Web MIDI), connect the FM-1 by
+   USB, allow MIDI access and follow the installer. The built `.fwsc` is also attached to the workflow run.
+
+## Building and flashing
+
+Building works exactly as upstream Felucca; see [BUILDING.md](../BUILDING.md). In short, on Linux x86-64:
+
+```sh
+git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca.git
+cd Felucca
+git checkout ca1db43 && git submodule update    # the upstream commit the patch is made against
+git apply /path/to/felucca-canvas.patch        # or skip these three steps and unpack the full source tarball
+pip3 install Pillow fonttools
+tools/get_toolchain.sh                           # JieLi's clang for the pi32v2 CPU
+git clone --depth 1 --branch AC79NN_SDK_V1.2.1_2023-12-13 \
+    https://gitee.com/Jieli-Tech/fw-AC79_AIoT_SDK.git ~/fw-AC79_AIoT_SDK
+./build.sh                                       # -> build/felucca.fwsc
+tests/run_tests.sh                               # optional: the host test suite, CANVAS included
+```
+
+On macOS, install Docker Desktop first; the toolchain runs in a `linux/amd64` container (see BUILDING.md).
+
+To tell the build apart on the device, make a release build with a suffix: `./build.sh --release 1.8-cnv`. The menu
+then shows `v1.8-cnv`.
+
+Flash `build/felucca.fwsc` with Felucca's installer. The hosted web installer installs only upstream's release, so
+use one of these:
+
+- **Command line** (USB; `pip3 install mido python-rtmidi`):
+  `python3 tools/fm1_install.py build/felucca.fwsc`
+- **A local copy of the web installer** (Chrome or Edge; Web MIDI needs `localhost`):
+
+  ```sh
+  python3 web/make_site.py build/felucca.fwsc dev /tmp/felucca-site
+  cd /tmp/felucca-site && python3 -m http.server 8000
+  # open http://localhost:8000/webapp/installer/
+  ```
+
+If an install fails and the FM-1 no longer starts, recovery needs
+[FM-1-transporter](https://github.com/kurogedelic/FM-1-transporter) (see BUILDING.md).
+
+To go back, install an upstream Felucca release with the hosted web installer, or use its "Return to official
+V15/V16". A project
+saved with a CANVAS track uses engine 15, which upstream Felucca doesn't know, so upstream refuses to load that
+project rather than playing it wrongly. Projects without CANVAS tracks load anywhere.
+
+## Engine numbers
+
+CANVAS is engine **15** (`ENGI_CANVAS`). Engine 14 stays reserved for upstream's optional ADPCM engine; in builds
+without ADPCM it's a silent placeholder that's never offered. `FELUCCA_CANVAS=0 ./build.sh` builds the firmware
+without CANVAS, identical in behaviour to upstream.
+
+## Source map
+
+| File | What |
+| --- | --- |
+| `firmware/src/eng_canvas.c` | The engine: canvas storage, grain spawning and rendering, presets, cell packing |
+| `firmware/src/ui_canvas.c` | The CANVAS page: cursor, knobs, keys, LEDs, the emitting-cell display |
+| `firmware/src/ui_graph.c` `graph_canvas` | The grid drawing |
+| `firmware/src/ui_draw.c` | The page's four cards and its footer hint |
+| `firmware/src/project.c`, `up_fm6.c`, `upreset.c`, `ui.c` | Saving the cells: projects, user presets, undo, preset loads |
+| `firmware/src/seq.c` `CANVAS_KEYS` | The eight silent keys on the page (`song.grid` 4) |
+| `tests/canvas_test.c` | Engine tests and demo renders (`build/canvas_demo/`) |
+| `tests/ui_test.c` `test_canvas` | Page, keys, LEDs, persistence and undo tests |
